  "result": {
    "text": "92.3.MODULESANDPRAGMATA\nCHAPTER92.PERL56DELTA\nDB_File\nDB_File can now be built with Berkeley DB versions 1, 2 or 3. See ext/DB_File/Changes.\nDevel::DProf\nDevel:DProf, a Perl source code profiler has been added. See Devel:DProf and dprofpp.\nDevel::Peek\nThe Devel:Peek module provides access to the internal representation of Perl variables and data. It is a data\ndebugging tool for the XS programmer.\nDumpvalue\nThe Dumpvalue module provides screen dumps of Perl data.\nDynaLoader\nDynaLoader now supports a dl_unload_fileO function on platforms that support unloading shared objects using\ndlcloseO.\nPerl can also optionally arrange to unload all extension shared objects loaded by Perl. To enable this,build Perl\nwith the Configure option -Accflags=-DDL_UNLOAD_ALL_AT_EXIT. (This maybe useful if you are using Apache\nwith mod_perl.)\nEnglish\n$PERL_VERSION now stands for $ ^V (a string value) rather than for $] (a numeric value).\nEnv\nEnv now supports accessing environment variables like PATH as array variables.\nFcntl\nMore Fcntl constants added: F_SETLK64, F_SETLKW64,O_LARGEFILE for large file (more than 4GB) access\n(NOTE: the O_LARGEFILE is automatically added to sysopenO flags if large file support has been configured, as\nisthedefault),Free/Net/OpenBSD1ockingbehaviourflagsF_FLOCK,F_POSIX,LinuxF_SHLCK,and\nO_ACCMODE:the combined mask of O_RDONLY,O_WRONLY, and O_RDWR.The seekO/sysseekO) constants\nSEEK_SET, SEEK_CUR, and SEEK_END are available via the : seek tag. The chmodO/statO S_IF* constants\nand S_IS* functions are available via the :mode tag.\nFile::Compare\nA compare_textO function has been added, which allows custom comparison functions. See File::Compare.\nFile::Find\nFile:Find now works correctly when the wantedO function is either autoloaded or is a symbolic reference.\nA bug that caused File:Find to lose track of the working directory when pruning top-level directories has been\nfixed.\nFile:Findnow also supportsseveral other options to control its behavior.It canfollowsymbolic links if the\nfo1low option is specified. Enabling the no_chdir option will make File:Find skip changing the current\ndirectory when walking directories. The untaint flag can be useful when running with taint checks enabled.\nSee File::Find.\nFile::Glob\nThis extension implements BSD-style file globbing. By default, it will also be used for the internal implementation\noftheglobOoperator.SeeFile::Glob.\nFile::Spec\nNew methods have been added to theFile::Spec module: devnullO returns the name of the null device (/dev/null\non Unix) and tmpdirO the name of the temp directory (normally/tmp on Unix). There are now also methods to\nconvert between absolute and relative filenames: abs2relO and rel2absO. For compatibility with operating systems\nthat specify volume names in file paths, the splitpathO, splitdirO, and catdirO methods have been added.\n1431",
